              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Do you know?"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "image_footnote",
              "index": 3,
              "bbox": [
                0.233,
                0.133,
                0.45,
                0.236
              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "The amount of water vapour in the air is more on rainy days and hence rainy days are more humid."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.485,
            0.084,
            0.883,
            0.229
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "It is also a common observation that clothes dry slowly on a rainy day. On a rainy day, water evaporates slowly. If the amount of water in the air is already high (more "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "humidity",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "), water evaporates slowly."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.482,
            0.232,
            0.882,
            0.275
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "If you want to dry your clothes on a rainy day, how can you make it faster?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.289,
            0.494,
            0.314
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "8.6 Cooling Effect"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.253,
            0.321,
            0.884,
            0.469
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Aavi’s mother purchased a new matka (earthen pot) to replace the stainless steel pot for storing drinking water. Upon returning from school, Aavi notices the earthen pot and drinks water from it. Aavi expresses surprise and asks, “Why is the water in the earthen pot so cold? I never observed water getting cold in a stainless steel pot.” What do you think is the reason?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.247,
            0.48,
            0.3,
            0.497
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Now,"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.144,
            0.498,
            0.4,
            0.586
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "I can understand why we feel cooler if we sit under a fan! The wind helps the sweat to evaporate and cools us."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.402,
            0.469,
            0.884,
            0.597
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Water seeps through the surface of the earthen pot and evaporates, which imparts a cooling effect on the water. What are the other examples of cooling effect? Sprinkling water on the floor or the roof during summer to cool it, is another example."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.118,
            0.576,
            0.241,
            0.703
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 11,
              "bbox": [
                0.118,
                0.576,
                0.241,
                0.703
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_13_image_11.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.619,
            0.394,
            0.639
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "your hands?"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.382,
            0.597,
            0.882,
            0.638
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "How do you feel when you rub sanitiser on"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.253,
            0.639,
            0.884,
            0.703
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Let us perform Activity 8.9 to observe the cooling effect by making a simple and electricity-free model of pot-in-pot cooler."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.716,
            0.618,
            0.738
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Activity 8.9: Let us make a model"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.255,
            0.748,
            0.723,
            0.772
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Take two earthen pots of different sizes."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.256,
            0.776,
            0.851,
            0.798
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Fill the bottom of the larger pot with a layer of sand."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.082,
            0.898,
            0.118,
            0.914
          ],
